il]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]] or finely-[[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (100 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[Cookbook:Bacon|bacon]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* ½ cup (100 g) [[Cookbook:Prawn|prawn]], diced\n* ¼ cup (50 g) Char siu (barbecued pork), diced\n* ⅛ cup (25 g) [[Cookbook:Scallion|scallion]], diced\n* ¼ cup (50 g) [[Cookbook:Peas|peas]]\n* ½ cup (100 g) beaten [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* 3 cups (600 g) cooked [[Cookbook:rice|jasmine rice]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Jalapeno|jalapeno]], diced (optional)\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Heat the oil in a non-stick [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|skillet]], and fry the garlic until golden brown.\n# Add the bacon, prawn, and char siu, then cook slightly for 5 minutes.\n# Add the scallion, peas, and egg, and cook until all cooked. \n# Stir in the rice, salt, pepper and jalapeno.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes for fried rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bacon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shrimp]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using jalapeño chile]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Yeung Chow Fried Rice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 tbsp corn oil","sourceText":"3 tbsp corn oil","amountText":"3 tbsp corn oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tbsp minced or finely-chopped garlic","sourceText":"2 tbsp minced or finely-chopped garlic","amountText":"2 tbsp minced or finely-chopped garlic","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ cup (100 g) bacon, diced","sourceText":"½ cup (100 g) bacon, diced","amountText":"½ cup (100 g) bacon, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"i